## Analysis & Pre-Thinking

**Core Requirements:**
1. When `chat.id` changes, reset: selected files, selected model, and selected profiles in ChatInputBox
2. Modify ChatLLMModelSelector to support single-selection mode (only one item selectable, emit immediately when selected/deselected, close modal automatically)

**Strategic Approach:**
1. Update `ChatLLMModelSelector.vue` to pass `isSingleSelect` prop to Selector and modify selection behavior
2. Update `Selector.vue` to auto-close modal in single-select mode after selection/deselection
3. Add a watcher in `ChatInputBox.vue` to monitor `chat.id` changes and reset state

**Dependencies & Risks:**
- Selector already supports `isSingleSelect` prop (confirmed in code)
- Need to ensure auto-close doesn't interfere with other components using Selector
- Profile selector currently allows multi-select; confirm this should remain unchanged

**Target Files:**
1. `src/components/chat/ChatLLMModelSelector.vue` - Enable single-select and auto-close
2. `src/components/chat/Selector.vue` - Auto-close on single-select changes
3. `src/components/chat/ChatInputBox.vue` - Watch chat.id and reset state

