## Summary of Changes

**ChatLLMModelSelector.vue:**
- Added `:is-single-select="true"` prop to Selector for single-selection mode

**Selector.vue:**
- Modified `selectItem()` method to auto-close modal and immediately emit changes when in single-select mode
- Behavior: When user clicks item in single-select mode → selection updates, modal closes, parent receives updated items

**ChatInputBox.vue:**
- Added `chatId` prop to track chat identity changes
- Added watcher that triggers `resetInputState()` when chat ID changes
- New method `resetInputState()` emits signals to parent to clear: images, profiles, and model selection
- Parent component (Chat.vue or similar) should listen to these events and clear corresponding state

**Usage in parent component:**
```vue
<ChatInputBox
  :chat-id="chat.id"
  @reset-state="onResetInputState"
  @profiles-selected="selectedProfiles = $event"
  @model-changed="selectedModel = $event"
  @remove-image="images = []"
  ...
/>
```

